# Files that are not part of the deployed site.
#
# Vercel uploads the whole repository before building. The legacy PHP app is
# ~258 MB of it and none of it is served — `outputDirectory` is ui/dist, so only
# the React build and the /api functions ever reach a visitor. Excluding it makes
# deploys markedly faster and keeps the old source out of the build entirely.
#
# Nothing in ui/ or api/ references these paths. The two mentions of
# "admin/assets" and "Contact_Us.php" in ui/src are comments explaining where a
# design came from, not imports.

# The previous PHP application
admin/
oldWebsite/
include/
others/
tools/
assets/
*.php
style.css

# Pre-rendered snapshot of the old site, built from fake data
static/

# Local test harness — an in-process database and the API compiled for it.
# scripts/ is included here too: nothing on Vercel executes it, so uploading the
# dev server (which carries a fixed development password) is needless surface.
scripts/
.local-api/
.local-db/
.selfcheck/

# Design/source files that are not web assets
*.cdr
README.md
ADMIN.md
